# A COMPLEX RANGE FILLER ON AN ASSERTED EDGE (SPEC 5.3 L2, L4). range(r) is
# C ⊓ ∃p.E, normalized through a fresh name that the seed for r(a,b) must place
# on b. Then ∃p.E ⊑ F makes b an F, and G(b) with F disjoint from G is a
# contradiction. Expect: INCONSISTENT (exit 1).

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:C a owl:Class . :E a owl:Class . :F a owl:Class . :G a owl:Class .
:F owl:disjointWith :G .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty . :p a owl:ObjectProperty .
:r rdfs:range [ a owl:Class ; owl:intersectionOf ( :C [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :p ; owl:someValuesFrom :E ] ) ] .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :p ; owl:someValuesFrom :E ] rdfs:subClassOf :F .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual . :b a owl:NamedIndividual , :G .
:a :r :b .
